sections.grading:
Unclear grading criteria for group projects, the exam of reciting, and bad overall grading as SSC-CCC.

a) a mid-term exam (covering the first four lectures) (30%);
b) a project presentation (20%);
c) a project essay (20%);
d) a final exam (covering the last four lectures) (30%).
I got 86 out of 100 in midterm (more than 1 SD above mean), 74 out of 100 in final (mean: 70.65),  93 out of 100 in presentation (upper: 91, high: 95), unknown grading for essay and end up with B+.

The most disgusting thing is that they open for paper checking but the only explanation is this is the objective answer, you need to accept. But actually, some of the answers are contradicted  from what Prof. has said in the course and TA will say he can't remember. Other answers like fill in the blanks, if you use similar wording but not the exact word on the PPT, TA will say he remembers the exact word Prof. used and you are wrong.

For group projects, there are no clear grading criteria.
